<item><title>Agadez governorate ties fuel sales to papers and purchase caps</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/agadez-governorate-ties-fuel-sales-to-papers-and-purchase-1dc6b6/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/agadez-governorate-ties-fuel-sales-to-papers-and-purchase-1dc6b6/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>From 1 December, buyers must show road documents; car purchases are capped at 30 litres, while tricycles and motorcycles face cash limits.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:05:29 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/agadez-governorate-ties-fuel-sales-to-papers-and-purchase-1dc6b6/share.jpg" length="42108" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/agadez-governorate-ties-fuel-sales-to-papers-and-purchase-1dc6b6/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
